False Positive (FP): Model predicts crash, but no crash happens.
Result: Investors may sell unnecessarily.
False Negative (FN): Model predicts no crash, but a crash actually happens.
Result: Investors keep their investments and may suffer huge financial losses.

Since missing a real crash (FN) is much more costly than a false alarm (FP), the goal is to reduce False Negatives (FN).

Therefore, use Recall.

Reason:

Recall = Focuses on catching as many actual crashes as possible.
It minimizes False Negatives (FN).

Performance Metric: Recall
